# Build context for the WEB image is the repository root:
#
#   docker build -f apps/web/Dockerfile -t butler-web:dev .
#
# It cannot be `apps/web`, because the Next build needs the bun workspace
# manifests (root package.json + bun.lock) and packages/shared. Docker reads
# .dockerignore and never .gitignore, so this file is the only thing keeping the
# git objects, the host node_modules and the real .env out of the image layers.

.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
coverage
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Real credentials live in .env / .env.local; they must never enter a layer.
# Next also auto-loads .env files at build time, which would inline those values.
# Docker anchors a slashless pattern to the context root (unlike .gitignore), so
# each nested form needs its own `**/` rule.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Not inputs to the web build.
docs
infra
apps/worker
**/*.md
